From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sc8280xp: keep iris IOVAs out of the
 content-protection range

When it loads the firmware, the iris driver passes [0, 0x25800000) to TZ
as the video content-protection range (tz_cp_config_vpu2: pixel from 0,
non-pixel from 0x01000000). Only secure sessions may use those
addresses. The driver limits its DMA mask to 0xe0000000 but nothing
keeps the IOVA allocator out of the low range, and the allocator hands
out addresses from the top down. Once enough buffers are mapped, a
non-secure session gets IOVAs below 0x25800000, and the first VPU access
to such a buffer resets the SoC without any kernel message.

A browser page with several videos is enough to get there. In the DMA
trace, each 1080p H.264 session from the Codec2 V4L2 HAL had 260-310 MiB
mapped (8 to 11 of its 16 input buffers of 16 MiB, 20 capture buffers
of 3 MiB and about 71 MiB of internal buffers), and a 1440p session
about 735 MiB. With six 1080p sessions and one 1440p session, the lowest
iris IOVA reached 0x18000000 within one second, and the tablet reset
right after.

Reserve the range in the iris IOVA space with a reserved-memory node
that only has iommu-addresses. The downstream driver does the same
with a virtual-addr-pool of 0x25800000-0xe0000000. When the space runs
out, the DMA mapping fails instead: VIDIOC_QBUF or VIDIOC_STREAMON
returns an error and that decode session fails, and the SoC does not
reset. With this change the same page no longer resets the tablet, and
the lowest iris IOVA stays at 0x25800000.

The venus and iris bindings allow one memory-region item, so
dtbs_check will flag the second one until the binding takes it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi
index c9ebcd061..7805bdf03 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sc8280xp.dtsi
@@ -735,6 +735,18 @@ reserved-region@aeb00000 {
 			reg = <0 0xaeb00000 0 0x16600000>;
 			no-map;
 		};
+
+		/*
+		 * When it loads the firmware, the iris driver hands
+		 * [0, 0x25800000) to TZ as the video content-protection range
+		 * (pixel and non-pixel). A buffer of a non-secure session mapped
+		 * there resets the SoC as soon as the VPU touches it, so keep
+		 * the IOVA allocator above it, like the downstream
+		 * virtual-addr-pool.
+		 */
+		iris_cp_iova: reservation-iris-cp {
+			iommu-addresses = <&iris 0x0 0x0 0x0 0x25800000>;
+		};
 	};
 
 	smp2p-adsp {
@@ -4259,7 +4271,9 @@ &config_noc SLAVE_VENUS_CFG QCOM_ICC_TAG_ACTIVE_ONLY>,
 
 			operating-points-v2 = <&iris_opp_table>;
 			iommus = <&apps_smmu 0x2a00 0x400>;
-			memory-region = <&pil_video_mem>;
+			/* The firmware region must stay first: the driver loads it by index 0. */
+			memory-region = <&pil_video_mem>,
+					<&iris_cp_iova>;
 
 			status = "disabled";
 
